{
  "version": 1,
  "doc": "Reedhollow's Kirru (the Lead, 2026-10-30: the creatures track builds the Kirru crowd bodies, assets_src/crowd/kirru; characters keep the named Pell, Owa and the Kirru child). The clutch: eight bodies on the greybox's clutch_0..7 stage actors on the Shore, so the farewell-tide (B09) shows Kirru, not capsules (the stage actors stay hidden until the story shows them); the bodies alternate so no two neighbours in either line match. The watchers (R01: the Kirru are already watching from the platforms, very tall, very still): one on each house platform, facing the lagoon, each row's `at` making its stand-in at CrowdSpots/<id>. Pell is never inside (rule 3); the gate and the causeway are clear. `body` rows: Kirru wear no tints. Each row's `tuning`: the Kirru's eye height (2.05 m, the youngster's 1.45 m) so their look-ats meet the party's eyes, and their stillness (bible section 8; pell.md section 1): a slower look-about, a longer and rarer glance, a narrow idle pace. The vignettes (the Lead, 2026-10-30: the Act II towns lived in; ground probed against the zone's collision, 2026-10-30), still as the Kirru are and on the clips they have (Pell's idle and talk): three fishers on the ring's inner edge with their staffs out over the lagoon's mangrove water, heron-still; two talking in bouts on the south ring (a chat pair); a youngster at the ring's inner edge watching the fishers. The lagoon's middle and the shore stay clear for the farewell-tide. M5-A3P-1811 (act3_ch18.md K03 to K05, the farewell-tide again): from `ch17_complete` the platform watchers stand turned round, their backs to the lagoon (each `_tide` row is its watcher's own spot, turned 180 degrees); the watchers' own rows carry `not_flag` on the same flag.",
